    "created_at": "2026-09-17T11:16:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-17T11:17:38Z",
    "body": "> I'm also fairly confident that we end up hashing most resources for various purposes in any event (cache keys, etc)\r\n\r\nWe don't hash the contents of the file for cache keys, just the URL and cache partition metadata. And even then we don't use a cryptographic hash, because we don't need to.\r\n\r\nPrevious experiments with hashing cache contents have shown that it is slow enough to have a measurable performance impact.",
